}\b\f0\fs24  \b0 Define the term 'clause' with examples? http://vustudents.ning.com\par
\par
 \cf1 A group of words that contains a subject and verb, there are two types of clauses: independent and dependent (sometimes called subordinate). In discussing aspects of language, such as sentence variety, the word "clause" is valuable. The following groups of words are clauses: \par
\pard\li720 the ship sank \i (independent)\i0  \par
just before the iceberg struck the ship \i (dependent)\i0  \par
the first lifeboat in the water was only half full \i (independent)\i0  \par
\pard\cf0    \b\par
